/altar log <page number>

So each transaction will be indexed by town. Are they likely to be accessed frequently?
If a town's transaction log is accessed, it is likely to be accessed again soon. So when a town's transaction log is accessed, we want to cache it for a few minutes. We will also want to cache the next couple of pages as well, to make sure that they're in the RAM for quick access in case the player decides to access them as well (likely). This will keep the access times quick and reduce the amount of expensive database operations that need to be performed

/altar log 1
- Load in the first 3 pages. Display the first one, and keep them all cached.
- 5 minutes after the last time the altar log is accessed, the cache should be dumped
  - How can we handle this?
    - Probably a single process dedicated to checking the access times and if more than 5 minutes have passed, dumping them.

